==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|haira-|lang=ang}} from {{proto|Indo-European|kei-||koi-|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old High German {{term|her|hēr|lang=goh}} (German {{term|hehr||august, holy|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|hárr||grey|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐍃|tr=hais||torch|lang=got}}, Old Saxon {{term|her|hēr|lang=osx}}. Non-Germanic cognates include Sanskrit {{term|केतु|tr=ketu||light, torch|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/haːɹ/|lang=ang}}

===Adjective===
{{infl|ang|adjective|head=hār}}

# Grey-haired, [[old]] and [[grey]], [[venerable]].

